livers. So, in foundation, we have the concept of neural network. What are perceptrons? Single layer, multi layer perceptron. And then what is the funda of bias weights? This is very basic. You should know this. Because you can't directly study the concept of neural network. Until you understand these things. And apart from this, if I tell you a little thing, in mathematics, if I say basic of linear algebra, or say probability, or say stats, or even say python, then you should know these things. After that, you do a little deep diving in deep learning. So, you will be able to do deep diving only when you have done the basics. If you have ever seen a video on deep diving, then what happens in deep diving? We go under the sea. So, it's not like you jump straight and reach the bottom. You put all the equipment, and then you go. You go with the trainer. So, I am telling you the same thing. So, in college, university, exam, interview, wherever you are asked, this syllabus will help you a lot. So, we will cover all the topics one by one. So, activation function, loss function, then comes in optimization. How to optimize the output that is coming. So, here gradient is decent, Adam is there, overfitting is the concept. We have to learn all these things here. After that, we have the CNN funda, you should know the model of CNN. RNN model, and in this, you should know the concept of long short term memory. LSTM, then comes the funda of transformers, that is modern AI. Where attention mechanism is very important. Then, the architecture of which is parallel processing, that should be understood. Then, we have the models, GPT, BERT, fine tuning, all these things should be done one by one. So, this is linked, you will reach the advanced level only if you start from basics. And in the last, we have GAN, what is generator, what is discriminator, adversarial losses, encoder, decoder, latent space, and even object detection, YOLO. If you are given a picture, you have to detect the obj